# The read-side capture contract, at the points that carry a source position.
#
# These five types are what every connector adapter implements and what the runtime calls, so a change
# here reaches code that is not in this repository. The failure this file exists to catch is narrower
# than "the contract changed": it is a position, or the run it belongs to, quietly ceasing to be
# threaded.
#
#   - cdc losing its start, so the port decides where to begin for a caller who never said;
#   - the snapshot seam narrowed, or removed, so a caller has to invent the position instead;
#   - a delivered run losing the position the source stated for it, so the durable read offset has
#     nothing to advance on and every run begins again from where the last one started;
#   - the delivered run narrowed back to a single change, so the grouping the source read in is gone
#     before anyone downstream can see it. Nothing looks wrong afterwards -- the same changes arrive in
#     the same order -- but every cost that is paid per act rather than per change is paid once per
#     change again, a durable write of the change above all, and no later code can put the run back
#     together because the only thing that knew where its edges were has already returned.
#
# All four compile. All four leave the rest of the build green. All four produce a pipeline that runs
# and reports healthy, while silently dropping changes, re-reading them, or paying N times over for
# them.
#
# Updating this file is therefore a decision, not a formality: say which of the four above is not being
# reintroduced, or say what replaces it.

